    "html": "<p><strong>Workflow 2 — Regional Analysis by Hydrologic Unit Code (HUC)</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Goal:</strong> Summarize sites and literature within a basin/sub-basin by selecting an area that matches a <strong>HUC boundary</strong> (HUC-2 / 4 / 6 / 8). <strong>Use this workflow when:</strong> You’re scoping sediment management needs or knowledge gaps for a watershed or district area. <strong>What you’ll get:</strong> A basin-focused set of Sites + associated Site Literature, plus relevant General Literature.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Step 1: Turn on the HUC layer you need</strong></p><p>Open the <strong>Layer List / Reference Layers</strong> control. Turn on the desired HUC layer (HUC-2, HUC-4, HUC-6, or HUC-8). <strong>Tip:</strong> Start with a larger HUC (e.g., HUC-4) for screening, then move to smaller units for detail. <strong>Result:</strong> HUC boundaries appear on the map.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Step 2: Navigate to your basin (Bookmarks or pan/zoom)</strong></p><p>Use <strong>Bookmarks</strong> (if available) to jump to a region, <strong>OR</strong> Pan/zoom the map to your basin of interest. <strong>Result:</strong> The basin boundary is visible and ready for selection.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Step 3: Use Spatial Selection to capture sites in the HUC</strong></p><p>Activate the <strong>Spatial Selection</strong> tool (near the search/tools area). Draw a polygon by roughly tracing the HUC boundary (you don’t need to be perfect). <strong>What happens next:</strong> Any sites intersecting your polygon are selected automatically. <strong>Result:</strong> The Selected Data and tables update to your region.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Step 4: Confirm the selection in the Sites tab</strong></p><p>In the <strong>Data Table</strong>, open the <strong>Sites</strong> tab. Confirm the number and distribution of selected sites matches your intent. <strong>Tip:</strong> If you got too many or too few, redraw the polygon or adjust the map scale. <strong>Result:</strong> You have a clean basin-based site set.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Step 5: Review Site Literature for the basin</strong></p><p>Switch to <strong>Site Literature</strong>. Scan for repeated themes (e.g., dredging vs drawdown, fish passage, water quality, modeling approaches). <strong>Result:</strong> You’ve identified what’s been studied in the basin—and what hasn’t.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Step 6: (Optional) Use filters to focus within the region</strong></p><p>Open <strong>Keyword Filters</strong> and refine within the selected HUC (examples: Sediment Source = bank erosion; Ecological Concern = water quality; Analysis = sediment transport modeling). <strong>Result:</strong> You’re narrowing the basin results to your technical question.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Step 7: Export basin results (sites + literature)</strong></p><p>Export <strong>Sites</strong>, <strong>Site Literature</strong>, and/or <strong>General Literature</strong> based on your current selection and filters. <strong>Result:</strong> You have a basin summary dataset for offline analysis, reporting, or comparison across HUCs.</p>"
